.TH DANBY-DIVING 1
.SH NAME
danby-diving \- translational and rotational motion of a diver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/diving
.SH MODEL
The centre of mass follows a drag-affected projectile while angular momentum
rotates the body.  Tucking reduces the effective moment of inertia and therefore
increases angular speed for fixed angular momentum.
.SH DISPLAY
The linked body rotates about its moving centre of mass.  Height and completed
rotations are plotted against time.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/diving.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR mechanism (2)
